1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,321
The build is red. You click rerun. It goes green. Nobody looks at what happened.

2
00:00:05,871 --> 00:00:07,471
Tomorrow it is red again.

3
00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:07,855
Rerun.

4
00:00:07,855 --> 00:00:08,239
Green.

5
00:00:08,239 --> 00:00:09,199
Within a month,

6
00:00:09,199 --> 00:00:13,359
the whole team has learned one thing: red does not mean anything.

7
00:00:13,909 --> 00:00:16,367
That is the real cost of a flaky test.

8
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:18,177
It does not just waste time.

9
00:00:18,177 --> 00:00:22,187
It teaches people to ignore the one signal that protects them.

10
00:00:22,737 --> 00:00:24,953
Today you learn to find the cause.

11
00:00:24,953 --> 00:00:25,279
Time,

12
00:00:25,279 --> 00:00:25,996
randomness,

13
00:00:25,996 --> 00:00:26,387
order,

14
00:00:26,387 --> 00:00:27,430
and environment.

15
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:30,559
You see a test pass and fail with the same code.

16
00:00:30,559 --> 00:00:33,297
And a lab judges whether your fix is real.

17
00:00:34,847 --> 00:00:36,276
Here is what to expect.

18
00:00:36,826 --> 00:00:41,306
One: what a flaky test is, and the four causes behind almost all of them.

19
00:00:41,856 --> 00:00:44,587
Two: how to fix each cause, instead of hiding it.

20
00:00:45,137 --> 00:00:48,742
Three: what never to do, and what to do while the fix is waiting.

21
00:00:49,292 --> 00:00:51,811
Then a live demo with real pytest.

22
00:00:51,811 --> 00:00:54,049
A random failure you can replay.

23
00:00:54,049 --> 00:00:55,728
A test that fails alone.

24
00:00:55,728 --> 00:00:58,316
A test that only works in one folder.

25
00:00:58,866 --> 00:01:00,331
And a lab with six checks,

26
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:04,050
including two planted bugs that your fixed tests must still catch.

27
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:09,198
A flaky test passes and fails on the same code.

28
00:01:09,198 --> 00:01:11,439
So the code is not the only input.

29
00:01:11,439 --> 00:01:12,955
Something else changes.

30
00:01:12,955 --> 00:01:14,932
There are four usual suspects.

31
00:01:15,482 --> 00:01:16,113
The clock.

32
00:01:16,113 --> 00:01:18,131
The test reads the current time.

33
00:01:18,131 --> 00:01:20,150
It passes at ten in the morning,

34
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:21,790
and fails at ten at night,

35
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:22,736
or on a Sunday,

36
00:01:22,736 --> 00:01:24,250
or in another time zone.

37
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,550
Randomness.

38
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:26,163
The test,

39
00:01:26,163 --> 00:01:26,982
or the code,

40
00:01:26,982 --> 00:01:28,481
makes a random choice.

41
00:01:28,481 --> 00:01:29,845
Most runs are lucky.

42
00:01:29,845 --> 00:01:31,072
Some runs are not.

43
00:01:31,622 --> 00:01:32,037
Order.

44
00:01:32,037 --> 00:01:35,012
One test leaves something behind: a global,

45
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:35,496
a file,

46
00:01:35,496 --> 00:01:35,911
a row.

47
00:01:35,911 --> 00:01:37,779
Another test depends on it.

48
00:01:37,779 --> 00:01:38,678
Run it alone,

49
00:01:38,678 --> 00:01:40,062
or in another order,

50
00:01:40,062 --> 00:01:41,030
and it breaks.

51
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:42,396
Environment.

52
00:01:42,396 --> 00:01:44,029
The test needs a folder,

53
00:01:44,029 --> 00:01:44,506
a file,

54
00:01:44,506 --> 00:01:44,982
a port,

55
00:01:44,982 --> 00:01:45,662
a network,

56
00:01:45,662 --> 00:01:46,343
or a tool.

57
00:01:46,343 --> 00:01:47,975
It works on one machine,

58
00:01:47,975 --> 00:01:49,132
and nowhere else.

59
00:01:49,682 --> 00:01:54,247
Four causes. And all four mean the test depends on something it does not control.

60
00:01:55,797 --> 00:02:00,618
The fix is always the same idea. Take control of the thing the test depends on.

61
00:02:01,168 --> 00:02:03,216
For the clock: pass the time in.

62
00:02:03,216 --> 00:02:04,816
A test with a fixed date,

63
00:02:04,816 --> 00:02:05,904
a Monday at nine,

64
00:02:05,904 --> 00:02:07,952
gives the same answer every day,

65
00:02:07,952 --> 00:02:09,168
in every time zone.

66
00:02:09,718 --> 00:02:11,509
For randomness: replace it.

67
00:02:11,509 --> 00:02:13,897
A fake call that fails exactly once,

68
00:02:13,897 --> 00:02:14,627
on purpose,

69
00:02:14,627 --> 00:02:17,479
is better than a call that fails sometimes.

70
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:18,540
Or fix the seed,

71
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:19,402
and print it,

72
00:02:19,402 --> 00:02:21,260
so you can replay a failure.

73
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:26,866
For order: no shared state. Every test builds what it needs, and leaves nothing behind.

74
00:02:27,416 --> 00:02:30,018
For environment: use a temporary folder.

75
00:02:30,018 --> 00:02:31,514
pytest gives you one,

76
00:02:31,514 --> 00:02:32,620
called tmp_path,

77
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:33,986
fresh for every test.

78
00:02:34,536 --> 00:02:36,798
Make the cause visible. Then remove it.

79
00:02:38,348 --> 00:02:41,377
Now what not to do. There are four tempting answers.

80
00:02:41,927 --> 00:02:42,552
Rerun it.

81
00:02:42,552 --> 00:02:46,233
Many pipelines can retry a failed test automatically.

82
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:47,900
It turns red into green,

83
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,428
and hides the problem.

84
00:02:49,428 --> 00:02:51,165
The test is still broken.

85
00:02:51,715 --> 00:02:52,201
Skip it.

86
00:02:52,201 --> 00:02:53,660
The test no longer runs,

87
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:55,726
so it no longer protects anything.

88
00:02:55,726 --> 00:02:58,157
And skipped tests are rarely un-skipped.

89
00:02:58,707 --> 00:02:59,627
Quarantine it.

90
00:02:59,627 --> 00:03:00,876
This one is honest,

91
00:03:00,876 --> 00:03:02,124
if it is temporary.

92
00:03:02,124 --> 00:03:03,044
Move it aside,

93
00:03:03,044 --> 00:03:03,964
with an owner,

94
00:03:03,964 --> 00:03:04,555
a ticket,

95
00:03:04,555 --> 00:03:05,278
and a date.

96
00:03:05,828 --> 00:03:06,235
Fix it.

97
00:03:06,235 --> 00:03:07,107
Find the cause,

98
00:03:07,107 --> 00:03:08,211
take control of it,

99
00:03:08,211 --> 00:03:10,187
and prove the test can still fail,

100
00:03:10,187 --> 00:03:11,524
when the code is wrong.

101
00:03:12,074 --> 00:03:14,997
A fixed flaky test is a test you can trust again.

102
00:03:16,547 --> 00:03:21,624
Go to the lab folder.

103
00:03:23,174 --> 00:03:25,073
Look around.

104
00:03:25,623 --> 00:03:27,031
Our scheduling code,

105
00:03:27,031 --> 00:03:28,369
cartsched.py,

106
00:03:28,369 --> 00:03:29,355
and the tests.

107
00:03:29,355 --> 00:03:30,623
And a demo folder.

108
00:03:30,623 --> 00:03:31,045
First,

109
00:03:31,045 --> 00:03:32,876
a flaky test I can replay.

110
00:03:33,426 --> 00:03:39,144
Read the test.

111
00:03:39,694 --> 00:03:40,657
A retry helper,

112
00:03:40,657 --> 00:03:42,968
and a call that fails half the time,

113
00:03:42,968 --> 00:03:43,610
at random.

114
00:03:43,610 --> 00:03:44,445
Two attempts.

115
00:03:44,445 --> 00:03:45,216
So it fails,

116
00:03:45,216 --> 00:03:46,243
one run in four.

117
00:03:46,793 --> 00:03:52,852
Run it eight times.

118
00:03:53,402 --> 00:03:54,103
Six pass.

119
00:03:54,103 --> 00:03:56,131
Seeds four and seven fail.

120
00:03:56,131 --> 00:03:56,911
Same code.

121
00:03:56,911 --> 00:03:57,690
Same test.

122
00:03:57,690 --> 00:04:00,186
Only the random numbers changed.

123
00:04:00,736 --> 00:04:03,872
Replay seed four.

124
00:04:04,722 --> 00:04:05,213
Failed.

125
00:04:05,213 --> 00:04:05,634
Again,

126
00:04:05,634 --> 00:04:06,265
it fails.

127
00:04:06,265 --> 00:04:09,843
A flaky failure became a failure you can reproduce,

128
00:04:09,843 --> 00:04:10,544
on demand.

129
00:04:10,544 --> 00:04:12,018
Now you can debug it.

130
00:04:12,568 --> 00:04:17,538
Test alone.

131
00:04:19,288 --> 00:04:24,515
Failed, alone. It only passes when the test before it has run. That is hidden state.

132
00:04:25,065 --> 00:04:30,078
Change folder.

133
00:04:30,628 --> 00:04:33,935
Run from there.

134
00:04:36,585 --> 00:04:37,015
Failed.

135
00:04:37,015 --> 00:04:38,734
It reads config.json,

136
00:04:38,734 --> 00:04:40,208
from the current folder.

137
00:04:40,208 --> 00:04:43,156
It only works when you stand in the right place.

138
00:04:43,706 --> 00:04:47,695
Back.

139
00:04:48,245 --> 00:04:53,280
Time zones.

140
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:58,459
Another zone.

141
00:04:59,009 --> 00:04:59,900
Different hours.

142
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,461
A test that reads the clock sees one of these.

143
00:05:02,461 --> 00:05:04,577
Which one depends on where you run it.

144
00:05:05,127 --> 00:05:12,124
The fix.

145
00:05:30,874 --> 00:05:35,696
No random. A list counts the calls. The first call fails. The second works.

146
00:05:36,246 --> 00:05:40,320
Replay seed four.

147
00:05:41,370 --> 00:05:45,701
Passed. And it passes for every seed, because nothing is random any more.

148
00:05:46,251 --> 00:05:50,838
Where am I?

149
00:05:51,388 --> 00:05:53,585
Zero out of six. Your starting line.

150
00:05:54,135 --> 00:05:56,098
Clean up.

151
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:58,504
Removed. Nothing left behind.

152
00:06:00,054 --> 00:06:03,894
Your lab task: fix the flaky tests, for real. Six checks.

153
00:06:04,444 --> 00:06:05,998
Do not change the code,

154
00:06:05,998 --> 00:06:07,011
only the tests.

155
00:06:07,011 --> 00:06:08,227
Pass a fixed time.

156
00:06:08,227 --> 00:06:09,308
Use a fake call.

157
00:06:09,308 --> 00:06:10,254
Use tmp_path.

158
00:06:10,254 --> 00:06:11,335
No shared state.

159
00:06:11,885 --> 00:06:16,471
One and two: the suite passes twenty times in a row, and in three time zones.

160
00:06:17,021 --> 00:06:19,830
Three and four: it passes from another folder,

161
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:21,539
and every test passes alone.

162
00:06:21,539 --> 00:06:22,760
At least five tests.

163
00:06:23,310 --> 00:06:27,065
Five: no clock, no random, no sleep, and no skip or xfail.

164
00:06:27,615 --> 00:06:30,479
Six: the judge plants two bugs in the code.

165
00:06:30,479 --> 00:06:32,278
Your tests must catch both.

166
00:06:32,278 --> 00:06:33,277
Then lab check,

167
00:06:33,277 --> 00:06:34,676
until six out of six.

168
00:06:36,726 --> 00:06:39,521
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

169
00:06:40,071 --> 00:06:41,535
One: the repository,

170
00:06:41,535 --> 00:06:45,855
github.com/it-waves/devops-ai,

171
00:06:45,855 --> 00:06:48,199
in the folder academy/lab.

172
00:06:48,749 --> 00:06:54,722
Two: the files, lab143.sh, and shortcuts143.sh.

173
00:06:55,272 --> 00:07:00,733
Three: install it, with sudo install, into /usr/local/sbin/.

174
00:07:01,283 --> 00:07:03,107
Four: load the short names,

175
00:07:03,107 --> 00:07:06,215
with source shortcuts143.sh.

176
00:07:06,215 --> 00:07:07,026
Then lab up,

177
00:07:07,026 --> 00:07:07,701
lab check,

178
00:07:07,701 --> 00:07:08,579
and lab down.

179
00:07:09,129 --> 00:07:14,399
Five: you need Python 3, and pytest. One apt install line gives you both.

180
00:07:14,949 --> 00:07:20,751
Six: it only touches /opt/lab143. Lab down removes everything.

181
00:07:21,301 --> 00:07:22,944
The link is in the description.

182
00:07:24,994 --> 00:07:28,642
Pass or fail rubric. Six points. All six to pass.

183
00:07:29,192 --> 00:07:31,624
One: the suite passes twenty runs in a row.

184
00:07:32,174 --> 00:07:34,350
Two: it passes in three time zones.

185
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,927
Three: it passes from another folder.

186
00:07:37,477 --> 00:07:39,653
Four: every test passes on its own.

187
00:07:40,203 --> 00:07:43,317
Five: no clock, random, sleep, skip or xfail.

188
00:07:43,867 --> 00:07:46,214
Six: the tests catch two planted bugs.

189
00:07:46,764 --> 00:07:48,065
Pass means all six.

190
00:07:50,115 --> 00:07:51,886
Your turn, on your own machine.

191
00:07:52,436 --> 00:07:57,321
One: lab up. Read the task file. Run the tests a few times, and see them fail.

192
00:07:57,871 --> 00:08:01,732
Two: fix the clock test. Pass a fixed date, and test the edges.

193
00:08:02,282 --> 00:08:06,826
Three: fix the retry test with a fake call. Test the success, and the give up.

194
00:08:07,376 --> 00:08:11,600
Four: fix the config test with tmp_path, and remove the shared state.

195
00:08:12,150 --> 00:08:15,628
Five: lab check, until six out of six. Then lab down.

196
00:08:16,178 --> 00:08:18,012
Pause the video, and begin now.

197
00:08:33,562 --> 00:08:34,437
Quick check.

198
00:08:34,987 --> 00:08:37,632
What are the four usual causes of a flaky test?

199
00:08:38,182 --> 00:08:40,699
Why is rerunning a failed test not a fix?

200
00:08:41,249 --> 00:08:43,105
How does a fixed seed help you debug?

201
00:08:43,655 --> 00:08:45,895
How do you prove a fixed test can still fail?

202
00:08:46,445 --> 00:08:52,653
Objective covered: MC15, objective eight. Flaky and environment dependent tests.

203
00:08:53,203 --> 00:08:55,273
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

204
00:09:05,823 --> 00:09:09,876
Next: the testing mastery scenario, the whole domain in one lab.

205
00:09:10,426 --> 00:09:13,754
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
